From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: jz4780: select the X1000 profile for the T31 controller

The T31 I2C controller has the 64-entry FIFO, the X1000 SDA hold
register at 0x7c and no STPHLD bit; the vendored 3.10 driver is built
with CONFIG_I2C_FIFO_LEN=64. The DT lists t31-i2c with a jz4780
fallback, so the driver currently binds the JZ4780 profile (16-entry
FIFO, STPHLD/stop-hold path). Register reads can then succeed while
the sensor init write array times out ("write wait timeout") and the
adapter never disables cleanly (ENSTA stuck at 1).

Match "ingenic,t31-i2c" explicitly and reuse the X1000 profile.

---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-jz4780.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-jz4780.c
@@ -754,6 +754,7 @@
 static const struct of_device_id jz4780_i2c_of_matches[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4770-i2c", .data = &jz4780_i2c_config },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4780-i2c", .data = &jz4780_i2c_config },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t31-i2c", .data = &x1000_i2c_config },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,x1000-i2c", .data = &x1000_i2c_config },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
